HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1cae2ae5, "` \342\200\224 clang read the header's struct and it has no such field");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1d6ae2a9, "a group's `record` IS the header's struct (\302\2474.19), so a field is named exactly as the header names it \342\200\224 correct the spelling, or name the header that gives `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_198788f6, "` a `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2da8f4d0, "not a flex assertion");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3cfd5bc4, "` gives `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2a40295c, "` no size \342\200\224 it is written there with empty brackets, so it is not a field this record can name at any length");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2d2bc957, "leave `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1c03abd2, "` out and write the `record` `partial` (\302\2474.19): what is left is the header's struct minus a member C itself does not size, and those bytes are reached through the functions the header declares for them");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2c082cc2, "with const-qualified data member '");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_645e4d98, "not a const-member line");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1fb1c18d, "ffi_const_field");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_29024863, "` as `const`, so C refuses to assign a `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_37905354, "` once it exists \342\200\224 and building one here is that assignment");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4a4d0d8e, "the `const` is the header's decision and no spelling on this line changes it: every Heroes value is built by assignment, so a struct C will not let you assign is a struct you take FROM the library rather than make. Ask a function the group declares for one, or drop the field and mark the `record` `partial` if you only need to read the others");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_69afd660, "no group record declares this member");
