HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_548c7b28, "a parameter");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_fc84968, "ffi_callback_type");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_40b136af, " of `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6d850ef6, "` is not the callback the header declares \342\200\224 clang read the header, and it says `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4524c15b, "\302\2474.19: a callback is declared with the header's own parameter and result types \342\200\224 each parameter at its width and sign, and `()` where the header says void");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_484f9e65, "a pointee the header marks `const` has no spelling here unless it is `const char *`, which is `cstr` \342\200\224 design.md Part 8 wart 19 names this and the four causes measured beside it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3d0b4c7a, "and C would convert the value in silence");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5a4e1aed, "and the two do not convert");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_74dc8569, "and the precision the header expects is lost before the call");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_241ac94a, "and C would drop the fraction in silence");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1405a546, "and C would round large values in silence");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_76937030, "ffi_freer_type");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_72066ad6, "` cannot free a string: the header takes `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_17487c7d, "`, and a freer for an `owned` `cstr` is handed the string's own bytes");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1e5ec359, "\302\2474.19: the compiler calls this function for you, so it is checked against the header the way your own call would be \342\200\224 and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5ec2a9e9, "` is not what a string is");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2abeb16e, "name the function that frees THIS string \342\200\224 `free` for `strdup`, `sqlite3_free` for SQLite's own \342\200\224 or drop the `owned` mark and free it yourself");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_ccf254, " the header's `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6c1001b, "` \342\200\224 clang read the header, ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_70e61340, "\302\2474.19: a parameter is declared as what the header says. `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5150ddd1, "` has no name in this language \342\200\224 if it is a struct, declare it as a `record` inside this same `extern` group and the header owns its layout");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4b36102a, "\302\2474.19: a result may be wider than C's, and a parameter is declared at the header's own width and sign. Declare it `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_322bf5af, "`, and convert at the call where the value is known to fit");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3ce6352e, "declare it `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_642854f4, "not a qualifier line");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_688dcb8b, "a marked `@cstr` owns what C writes there");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7bef8b75, "ffi_writable_parameter");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1a93c4b1, "` is declared `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6b968494, "`, and the header says `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_f7f4783, "` \342\200\224 C does not promise to leave it alone");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_737856d6, "\302\2474.20: `s.cstr()` lends the string's own bytes, and they may be shared with other values \342\200\224 a C write through them changes values this program never passed to C, and on a literal it aborts");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3702d241, "declare it `ptr` and give `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5540bf3c, "` a buffer C owns, then read the result back");
